([10:15 AM] REED: Please state your name and role.) Tj T*
([10:15 AM] CHEN: Bob Chen, IT Systems Administrator for Meridian Tech.) Tj T*
([10:16 AM] REED: Can you walk us through your whereabouts on the evening of) Tj T*
(October 12?) Tj T*
([10:16 AM] CHEN: I arrived at Building 4 at 8:00 PM for scheduled server) Tj T*
(maintenance. Around 9:30 PM, I stepped out to pick up takeout from the deli) Tj T*
(down the street. I came back around 10:20 PM and worked at my terminal until) Tj T*
(1:00 AM.) Tj T*
([10:17 AM] REED: Where was your master keycard during that time?) Tj T*
([10:17 AM] CHEN: I had my physical master keycard in my wallet all evening) Tj T*
(and never lent it to anyone. I keep it chained to my belt loop at all times.) Tj T*
([10:18 AM] REED: Did you enter Server Room B during the night?) Tj T*
([10:18 AM] CHEN: No, I worked strictly from my office on Floor 2. I had no) Tj T*
(reason to visit Server Room B because my remote SSH console was functioning) Tj T*
(properly.) Tj T*
([10:19 AM] REED: Did you authorize any subcontractor or outside technician to) Tj T*
(access the server vault?) Tj T*
([10:19 AM] CHEN: No, absolutely not. Subcontractors are strictly prohibited) Tj T*
(from entering secure zones without an escort.) Tj T*
